            <ArticleTitle>Platelet function, coagulopathy, and impaired fibrinolysis in diabetes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>511-26</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Diabetes and the metabolic syndrome, including insulin resistance, that underlies it are hyper-coagulable states. Increased platelet reactivity,augmented activity of the coagulation system,and impaired fibrinolysis are characteristic and understood to a remarkable extent. In aggregate,these derangements contribute to accelerated atherosclerosis, premature coronary artery dis-ease, and a profound toll from both.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
